ne the slope of $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ at the point $(10,0).$" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318683 1113 #uuid "77be3a89-d855-50f1-9ab2-8a545dc34af5" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318683 1145 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(0,10).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}+4x+10 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{2}{3}x+4 \\\\ {f}^{′}(0) & =4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(0,10)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(10,0)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(10) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(10))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318685 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318686 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318687 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318688 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1000 #edb/ref 17592186318689 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1041 "selection" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1104 #edb/ref 17592186318686 13194139534905 true] [17592186318684 1110 #uuid "a79fa784-2df7-5911-89a7-a24e4f8099fb" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318685 1034 "\\frac{1}{10}" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534905 true] [17592186318685 1111 #uuid "fb7519bb-b47a-57e2-8892-57c435b02cb0" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318686 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534905 true] [17592186318686 1111 #uuid "60b0725e-ac88-5a08-b1fb-e1ff58195c78" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318687 1034 "1" 13194139534905 true] [17592186318687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534905 true] [17592186318687 1111 #uuid "c4c72983-c1